---
/*
 * /terms/ — Terms of Service.
 *
 * Terms for the open-design.ai site, accounts, and Open Design Cloud.
 * Local software is governed by the license shipped with that software.
 */
import Layout from '../../_components/sub-page-layout.astro';

const updated = 'July 23, 2026';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Terms of Service — Open Design',
  url: new URL('/terms/', Astro.site).toString(),
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Open Design', url: Astro.site?.toString() },
};
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Open Design"
  description="The terms that govern use of the open-design.ai website, accounts, and Open Design Cloud. Software licensing is governed separately."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1 class="legal-h1">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>These Terms govern your use of the website <a href="https://open-design.ai">open-design.ai</a>, Open Design accounts, and Open Design Cloud provided by <strong>Powerformer, Inc.</strong> (“Open Design”, “we”, “us”). Open Design Cloud includes account access, wallet credits, API key management, CLI authorization, model request routing, usage metering, and billing. By using the site, an account, or Cloud services, you agree to these Terms. Local Open Design software is governed solely by the license and notices shipped with the applicable copy; these Terms do not modify that software license.</p>

    <h2>1. The software is source-available</h2>
    <p>First-party material expressly covered by the root <a href="https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design/blob/main/LICENSE">Open Design Community License 1.0</a> is provided under a custom source-available license based on Apache License 2.0. Third parties need commercial authorization to operate Open Design for any external customer, embed it in another product or service, or offer it through OEM, resale, sublicensing, or white labeling. Frontend branding conditions also apply. The public software license does not require a Team subscription merely because multiple people use a customer-operated copy. Earlier copies released under the unmodified Apache License 2.0 remain under their original terms.</p>

    <h2>2. Local-first BYOK and hosted Cloud services</h2>
    <p>The local Open Design app is local-first and BYOK: you connect your own model-provider credentials, and your use of those providers is subject to their terms and pricing. You are responsible for the keys you configure and the costs they incur.</p>
    <p>Open Design Cloud provides hosted model routing, wallet credits, usage metering, and billing. Open Design may route requests to different upstream model or infrastructure providers based on availability, cost, latency, compliance, and operational policies. Models, prices, credits, providers, routes, and features may change. We will explain material changes through reasonable channels such as the site, in-app notices, or email.</p>
    <p>On the official service, Open Design may require an active Team plan before an invitation that would add a second person can be sent or accepted. The applicable pricing page, checkout, order, and account record define the included seats and service scope. Removing additional members does not by itself cancel a subscription or create a refund right.</p>

    <h2>3. Account and credential security</h2>
    <p>You must provide accurate information and protect accounts, passwords, API keys, CLI authorization codes, and access tokens. Activity through your account or credentials is treated as authorized by you. If you discover leakage, abnormal usage, or unauthorized access, you should disable the affected credential and notify Open Design immediately.</p>

    <h2>4. User content and compliance</h2>
    <p>You are responsible for prompts, files, images, code, input data, API requests, and your use of model outputs submitted through Open Design. You represent that you have lawful rights to process and submit that content and will not submit illegal, infringing, confidential, unauthorized, malicious, or policy-violating content.</p>
    <p>Without a separate written agreement, you must not submit specially regulated data such as health data, financial account data, identity documents, minors’ information, biometrics, precise location, full payment card data, or other sensitive personal information.</p>
    <p>You retain ownership of what you create with Open Design. Contributions you submit to the source-available project are licensed under the project’s license as described in its CONTRIBUTING guide.</p>

    <h2>5. Prohibited uses and high-risk contexts</h2>
    <p>You must not use the website, an Open Design account, Open Design Cloud, or another hosted service we provide for illegal activity, fraud, phishing, spam, malware, attacks, security bypass, privacy violations, intellectual property infringement, unlawful content generation, circumvention of model provider policies, or violations of export control or sanctions rules. Community spaces such as GitHub and Discord are also governed by their respective codes of conduct.</p>
    <p>Without Open Design’s written approval, our accounts and hosted services must not be used for high-risk automated decision-making involving medical, legal, financial, employment, credit, insurance, law enforcement, critical infrastructure, or personal safety contexts. This service restriction does not add a field-of-use restriction to separately licensed local software.</p>

    <h2>6. Model outputs</h2>
    <p>Model outputs may be inaccurate, incomplete, or unsuitable for your purpose. You are responsible for reviewing outputs and actions taken based on them. Open Design does not provide medical, legal, financial, investment, or other professional advice.</p>

    <h2>7. Wallet, recharge, and billing</h2>
    <p>Wallet credits are only for Open Design-supported model calls and related metered services. They are not cash and, unless required by law or stated in page rules, cannot be withdrawn or transferred. Purchasing or holding credits does not by itself provide Team access; a Team entitlement must be expressly included in the applicable plan, order, or account record. An insufficient or zero credit balance may stop metered calls, but does not by itself cancel an otherwise valid Team entitlement.</p>
    <p>Recharge, discounts, invoices, refunds, taxes, and disputes are governed by checkout pages, order records, campaign rules, and applicable law. Open Design may calculate charges based on model, tokens, media tasks, route, success status, pricing tables, and provider cost.</p>

    <h2>8. Limits, suspension, and termination</h2>
    <p>Open Design may apply limits to accounts, API keys, request rates, balances, models, endpoints, or risk behavior. Open Design may suspend, restrict, or terminate service for non-payment, abuse, legal risk, provider failure, security incidents, breach of terms, or regulatory requirements.</p>

    <h2>9. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>Third-party login, payment, security verification, email, cloud, and model providers are governed by their own terms and privacy policies. Open Design does not guarantee continuous availability of third-party services or assume responsibility beyond legal requirements for third-party model policies, pricing, latency, failures, or outputs.</p>

    <h2>10. Intellectual property and trademarks</h2>
    <p>“Open Design”, “Powerformer”, related logos, the hosted interface, service documentation, service design, and related intellectual property belong to Powerformer, Inc. or its licensors. Without authorization, you may not copy, modify, reverse engineer, resell, rent, sublicense, or use Open Design hosted services competitively. Nothing in this paragraph narrows permissions granted by the license that accompanies an applicable local Open Design software copy.</p>
    <p>Third-party names and brands referenced on the site, including for comparisons, belong to their respective owners and are used for identification only. You retain rights to your own content, but grant Open Design the processing rights necessary to provide, protect, bill, and improve the service.</p>

    <h2>11. No warranty</h2>
    <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, Open Design is provided as-is and as-available. We do not guarantee uninterrupted, error-free service or that Open Design will meet every business objective.</p>

    <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Powerformer, Inc. will not be liable for indirect damages, lost profits, data loss, business interruption, third-party service failures, or consequences of model outputs. This does not exclude or limit liability that cannot be excluded by law, including liability for intentional misconduct, gross negligence, personal injury where legally non-waivable, or mandatory consumer rights.</p>

    <h2>13. Updates</h2>
    <p>Open Design may update these Terms for the website, accounts, and hosted services. Material changes will be communicated through the page, in-app notice, or email. Continued use of those services after changes take effect means you accept the updated terms; if you do not agree, stop using the service. An update to these Terms does not change the license governing a software copy you already received.</p>

    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@open-design.ai">support@open-design.ai</a>, visit the <a href="https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design">Open Design GitHub repository</a>, or join the community <a href="https://discord.gg/mHAjSMV6gz">Discord</a>.</p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .legal {
      max-width: 720px;
    }
    .legal-h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 40px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      color: var(--ink, #262626);
    }
    .legal-meta {
      margin: 10px 0 32px;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--ink-mute, #595959);
    }
    .legal h2 {
      margin: 32px 0 12px;
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--ink, #262626);
    }
    .legal p,
    .legal li {
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--ink-soft, #434343);
    }
    .legal p {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
    }
    .legal a {
      color: var(--ink, #262626);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 2px;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
